item.text:
I use ages **40–80** and the stated input ranges to rank approximate shared log-odds changes; ranks can tie. The common core is age, clinical severity, treatment status, and a strong **l3 rise around 3–4**. Weak, inconsistent patterns are omitted.

The rounded surrogate predicts **15.1%**, versus **15.3%** averaged across the networks, at age 60, all binary inputs zero, and all labs five. Surgery describes treatment received during admission, rather than an admission measurement.

